your challenges  every once in a while if you're looking  for some upgrades so what perks should  you focus on they're all good for  different styles of play but here are  some general purpose ones useful for  everyone on the survivalist tree I would  definitely put points into harvest  master which doubles new rewards from  plants and animals which is great for  making money I'd also invest in all of  the health boost upgrades because this  game is pretty tough and on the base  health you go down real quick the repair  torch is a useful tool that lets you fix  up vehicles but you can also use it to  open up a safe on the renegade tree pick  up the parachute for when you need to  make a quick escape  off a helicopter and the wingsuit for  when you want to enjoy the lovely  Montana countryside both these give you  a lot more options in traversing Hope  County and they're just really fun to  use especially in combination with each  other for the assassin tree get grapples  so you can climb up grapple spots like  in Far Cry 4 and locksmith so you can  open safes and doors without needing a  key for the prepper tree grabbed journey  pack to increase your item inventory  additional holster gets to a third  weapon slot and weapons collector gets  you the fourth weapon slot you'll find  yourself wishing you could hold all  manners of guns so I recommend getting  these as quickly as possible money  doesn't just naturally accumulate as  quickly like a dozen previous Far Cry  games but you can still make a lot of  money if you know what to focus on  hunting and skinning animals is no  longer needed to craft things like a new  wallet so it's mainly meant as a way to  make money as I previously mentioned the  harvest master perk doubles your rewards  from animals so $100 feathers becomes  $200 and a doubled cougar skin Nets you  four hundred and fifty dollars you  should also keep your eye out for safes  inside buildings I mentioned before that  you'll need either the repair torch or  locksmith perk to open them but placing  an explosive on them also does the trick  the last method is the prepper stashes  these are really cool side missions  where you need to do some light  environmental puzzle solving to get  access to a pile of loot whether that's  swimming across the river and shooting  the lock off a door or navigating a barn  full of beehives  you're rewarded with a pile of phat cash  a couple magazines that give you free  perk points and sometimes other goodies  like a new weapon so definitely do the  prepper stashes not only are the rewards  well worth it but they are also some of  the best missions in the whole game  and speaking of missions it seems  Ubisoft has finally learned because Far  Cry 5 ditches their open-world  cookie-cutter formula for the first time  Far Cry has side missions like proper  Rio last side missions with unique  dialogue and gameplay for each one you  know like video games needs to have  [Music]  Stark aside far cry 5 side missions are  real good and well worth your time from  simple missions like saving people from  drugged up bears to letting cows have  sex to Marvin Gaye music so you can chop  off their testicles for the annual test  FST  [Music]  that is in fact a real thing in this  game you can't wait to pop one of those  juicy balls into my mouth  you also get some pretty sweet rewards  like new weapons or beefed up vehicles  with guns on them every side mission  I've done has been worth the time  whether it's a sweet reward or just  something really funny happened so I  recommend doing them all  [Music]  expanding off the buddy system all the  way back in Far Cry 2 and the resistant  stuff in farcry 4 farcry 5 has he robust  cast of characters to call in and help  you out which you'll need because I  mentioned before the game can be pretty  tough there are 9 specialists you'll  find throughout Hope County and you'll  need to complete a story mission for  them all of their missions are marked on  the map from the get-go so it's pretty  easy to find them  each buddy has two abilities associated  with them for example boomer the dog can  tag all nearby enemies and fetch a  weapon for you after they attack making  him both a useful Scout and a very good  boy there's a great variety from Nick  the pilot to grace the sniper with the  leadership perk you can have access to  two at a time letting you combo  characters for the perfect attack they  also each have their own perk that  lessens the cooldown time for getting  them back so pick that up for your  favorites  just remember to dismiss Nick before you  try and stealth a outpost because he  will give away your position with a  carpet bomb  outside of the specialist there are  three slots you can fill with civilians  that you save and then higher they also  have two abilities but these need to be  unlocked by getting kills with them the  abilities are random though so if you  don't like them you can always get rid  of them and then hire a new person so I  hope these tricks and tips help you out  when playing far cry if it wasn't clear  from my enthusiasm I think far cry 5 is  Ubisoft's best open-world game in years  and I'm still finding cool stuff all the  time like did you know you can pet dogs  video games are good again go play far  cry  [Music]

